// Crane supplementary IDL - not in webref.
// Origin: lane rep2 (2026-11-14), the user's ruling of 2026-11-14 ("yes"):
// Report and ReportBody are the Reporting spec's DICTIONARIES
// (w3c/reporting#284, merged 2025-06-11; WebKit 326027@main, PR #79766,
// merged 2026-11-07). It replaces specs/supplementary/reporting-interfaces.idl
// (the 2026-11-05 ruling's interfaces).
//
// The pinned webref defines Report, ReportBody and the bodies of CSP,
// Subresource Integrity, Permissions Policy, Deprecation, Intervention, Crash,
// Scripting Policy and Connection Allowlists as dictionaries; codegen reads
// them from specs/idl. The report types below have a body that no spec writes
// as IDL, so each is a dictionary here, inheriting ReportBody as the specs'
// bodies do. dom.reporting converts a report's body with its type's
// dictionary (Reporting §4.3 step 3 leaves "how to polymorphically
// initialize body?" open; WebKit converts each body with its own dictionary:
// Source/WebCore/Modules/reporting/Report.idl, whose body member is a union
// of the body dictionaries, and ReportingObserver.cpp
// dictionaryForReportBody). Dictionaries have no interface object, so
// nothing here is exposed to script.

// HTML 7.1.4 "queue a cross-origin embedder policy inheritance violation":
// a "coep" report of type "navigation" or "worker initialization" ("a new
// object containing" type, blockedURL and disposition). WebKit's dictionary
// and name (Report.idl).
dictionary COEPInheritenceViolationReportBody : ReportBody {
  DOMString type;
  USVString blockedURL;
  DOMString disposition;
};

// Fetch 3.7 "queue a cross-origin embedder policy CORP violation report": a
// "coep" report of type "corp" ("a new object containing" type, blockedURL,
// destination and disposition). WebKit's dictionary and name (Report.idl).
dictionary CORPViolationReportBody : ReportBody {
  DOMString type;
  USVString blockedURL;
  RequestDestination destination;
  DOMString disposition;
};

// Reporting §7.1 Generate Test Report: a "test" report's body, "a single
// string field" message. WebKit's dictionary and name (Report.idl).
dictionary TestReportBody : ReportBody {
  DOMString message;
};

// The "coop-access-violation" report Chromium queues on the accessing
// document's ReportingObservers (dom.coop_reporting): the members of its
// CoopAccessViolationReportBody
// (third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/coop_access_violation_report_body.idl
// and LocationReportBody). Chromium alone makes this report (wpt.fyi at
// 2358bd4835: html/cross-origin-opener-policy/reporting/access-reporting/
// reporting-observer.html Chrome 4/4, Firefox 0/4, Safari 0/4).
dictionary CoopAccessViolationReportBody : ReportBody {
  DOMString? sourceFile;
  unsigned long? lineNumber;
  unsigned long? columnNumber;
  DOMString type;
  DOMString property;
  DOMString openeeURL;
  DOMString openerURL;
  DOMString otherDocumentURL;
};
